        "location": "Auxiliary results L2-L5 and “Remaining main-goal obligations.”",
        "hypotheses": "The main objective quantifies over every allowable rational height and integer pair and requires all fifteen pairwise product-plus-one conditions.",
        "conclusion": "L2's common-neighbor parametrization and infinite-graph K4 formulation are not an all-height obstruction. L3's square-denominator conclusion requires coprime integer anchors; its counterexample demonstrates why the hypothesis matters. L4 concerns only the specified canonical point of order exactly three in a triple and does not cover other placements of integers in a sextuple. L5 gives false positives for a preliminary extension test, not a proof that the displayed quadruples have no other extensions. None resolves existence or nonexistence of the target sextuple."
